ik</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Beecher</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Goli</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Separation, identification, and quantification of carotenoids in fruits, vegetables and human plasma by high performance liquid chromatography</article-title><source>Pure Appl. Chem</source><year>1991</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>80</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16-marinedrugs-07-00045"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bradford</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A rapid and sensitive method for the quantitation of microgram quantities of protein utilizing the principle of protein-dye binding</article-title><source>Analyt. Biochem</source><year>1976</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>294</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">942051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-marinedrugs-07-00045"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berges</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A comparison of Lowry, Bradford and Smith protein assays using different protein standards and protein isolated from the marine diatom <italic>Thalassiosira pseudonana</italic></article-title><source>Mar. Biol</source><year>1993</year><volume>115</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>193</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b18-marinedrugs-07-00045"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sambrook</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fritsh</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Maniatis</surname><given-names>T</g